The Role of lru_cache
The all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model file lives on your hard drive (roughly an 80MB file). Loading an AI
 model involves reading that file, parsing the neural network architecture, and copying millions 
 of mathematical weights into your computer's RAM. This takes a noticeable chunk of time (around 
 0.5 to 1.5 seconds).

Without a cache, every single time your program calls _get_model(), it would destroy the old model 
and reload it from scratch.

pip install -e . 